<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khalid ibn al-Walid</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/642">642 CE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/7th-century">7th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Khalid ibn al-Walid was an Arab military commander of the early Islamic period, celebrated as one of the most successful generals of his age. Leading armies for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>, he played a central part in campaigns against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanian Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. His mobile tactics and victories helped secure the rapid expansion of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a> in the 630s.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khalid-ibn-al-walid.jpg" alt="Khalid ibn al-Walid" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Abdulhadi Najjar · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khalid_ibn_al-Walid_Mosque.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>…Battle of the Yarmuk in August 636 CE, where Arab forces under the command of Abu Ubayda and <b>Khalid ibn al-Walid</b>, perhaps the most gifted battlefield commander of the seventh century, defeated a large Byzantine army over six days, in tradition aided by a dust storm, delivered Syria…</blockquote><a href="/empire/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>After six days of fighting, the Muslim Arab army under <b>Khalid ibn al-Walid</b> destroyed the Byzantine forces near the River Yarmouk.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/august-20">20 August in history</a></li><li><blockquote>After a siege begun on 21 August, Damascus fell to the forces of the Rashidun Caliphate under <b>Khalid ibn al-Walid</b>.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/september-19">19 September in history</a></li><li><blockquote>The Azizan family, which claimed descent from the Arab general <b>Khalid ibn al-Walid</b>, ruled Jazirat ibn Umar (Cizre) and the Bohtan region on the Tigris from the late Middle Ages, their power predating the arrival of the Ottomans.</blockquote><a href="/state/emirate-of-bohtan">Emirate of Bohtan</a></li></ul></section>
<section class="enc-where enc-born"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Born and died</h2><p class="enc-born-p">Born in the Kingdom of Saudi Arabia. Died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/homs">Homs</a>, in what is now <a href="/countries/syria">Syria</a>. <span class="enc-born-src">Places as Wikidata records them.</span></p><figure class="st-locator enc-loc"><a href="/atlas?at=34.73,36.72&amp;year=632" aria-label="Homs on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5482 907 900 540" role="img" aria-label="Map: the place of death of Khalid ibn al-Walid"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5932 1177h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5932 1177h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks the place of death. <a href="/atlas?at=34.73,36.72&amp;year=632">What was here in 632 CE? &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></section>
